# `gcloud builds submit` (deploy/ingestion/cloudbuild.yaml) uploads this repo's
# working directory as the Cloud Build source archive BEFORE the build even
# starts -- it reads THIS file, not .dockerignore, for that upload step.
# deploy/ingestion/Dockerfile.worker only ever COPYs backend/ (plus needs
# deploy/ingestion/Dockerfile.worker itself, referenced via `-f` in
# cloudbuild.yaml). Allowlisting rather than blocklisting: this repo root
# accumulates large unrelated trees over time -- a full AutomationBench/.venv
# virtualenv (20,233 files, ~93% of the prior upload) was found sitting here
# with nothing excluding it, and a blocklist would need updating every time
# something new like that shows up. `!X/` + `!X/**` is the standard
# gitignore-syntax "un-ignore everything under X" idiom; gcloud parses this
# file with the same syntax.

*

!deploy/
!deploy/**

!backend/
!backend/**

# Re-exclude from the allowed trees what still shouldn't ship (mirrors
# .dockerignore, which gcloud does not read for this upload step).
backend/.env
backend/.venv/
backend/__pycache__/
backend/**/__pycache__/
backend/.pytest_cache/
backend/stealthlab_backend.egg-info/
backend/conflict_candidates.json
backend/*_results.json
backend/experiment_*
backend/after_*
backend/*.log
backend/*.jsonl
backend/scripts/dev_dashboard.py
